The root cause is a code snippet of the following form:
# x: f32[b, 8]
def f_jax(x): 
   return jnp.mean(x)

jax2tf.convert(f_jax, polymorphic_shapes=["b, ..."])(np.ones((3, 4)))

The issue is that jnp.mean tries to compute and divide by the size of x, which is not a constant.

import jax.numpy as jnp
from jax import custom_vjp
from jax import jit
from jax import jacrev
import time


@custom_vjp
@jit
def f(x):
  print("called f!")
  return jnp.sin(x)

@jit
def f_fwd(x):
  print("called f_fwd!")
  return f(x), jnp.cos(x)

@jit
def f_bwd(cos_x, y_bar):
  print("called f_bwd!")
  return (cos_x * y_bar,)

f.defvjp(f_fwd, f_bwd)

for i in range(5):
  start = time.time()
  print(jacrev(f)(3.0))
  print("duration", time.time()-start)
  print("============")
If you run the previous codes many times (for example 10),  you will different results for the same code. And different results imply random compiling customized jacrev function.

